Upstream derivation
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

Portions of this project are derived from:

    typesafe-mcp
    https://github.com/itsmostafa/typesafe-mcp
    Revision 0c9f35d9b1859189fc7e7d01947061f311ca6dde (v0.4.1)
    Copyright (c) 2026 Mostafa
    Licensed under the MIT License (see LICENSE)

The upstream MIT license and copyright notice are preserved in LICENSE and
apply to the derived portions.

What was derived, in internal/typesafe:

  * The overall request/response shape for POST /v1/systemone (state, model,
    questions map of {type, instructions, criteria}) and the three question
    types noul, choice and score, as expressed in upstream
    cmd/evaluate/tools.go.
  * The idea of retrying only 429 and 529 with exponential backoff and of
    capping the response body, from upstream cmd/evaluate/client.go.

What was deliberately changed or dropped, and why:

  * Not imported at all: cmd/evaluate/setup.go (agent registration),
    cmd/evaluate/update.go (self-update from a GitHub release),
    install.sh (remote installer), and the OpenRouter route in
    cmd/evaluate/main.go. This project talks to the official endpoint
    https://api.typesafe.ai/v1/systemone only, with the model pinned to
    jev-1.13.0, and never modifies the host it runs on.
  * Credentials are no longer read from TYPESAFE_API_KEY or
    OPENROUTER_API_KEY in the ambient environment. A dedicated,
    owner-provisioned key file is read instead, with ownership, mode, file
    type and content checks (see internal/typesafe/key.go).
  * Errors no longer carry the API response body, the request, the
    credential or any filesystem path. Upstream returned
    fmt.Errorf("evaluate: %s: %s", resp.Status, b); this project returns
    fixed, sentinel-wrapped messages instead (see internal/typesafe/errors.go).
  * Request validation is no longer limited to "the criteria shapes the API
    definitely refuses". Question ids, value kinds, nesting depth, element
    counts and byte sizes are all bounded before anything is sent.
  * Responses are parsed and revalidated field by field and re-serialized
    from the validated values, rather than forwarded as the raw body. The
    model pin is enforced on the way back as well as the way out, numbers
    must be real JSON numbers rather than quoted ones, distributions must
    be internally consistent with the choice or score they accompany, and a
    score legend is rebuilt from the criteria that were sent rather than
    copied from the reply.
  * The response cap is 128 KiB rather than 16 MiB, the request is capped at
    64 KiB, retries are capped at 2 rather than 3, the backoff is capped and
    cancellable, the whole call has a 30 second deadline, redirects are
    refused, and ambient HTTP proxy environment variables are ignored.
